    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2003-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring gives \\(2x^2 + 3x - 5 = (2x + 5)(x - 1),\\) so the roots are \\(-\\dfrac{5}{2}\\) and \\(1.\\)\n\nSince one root equals \\(1,\\) one of the two factors \\(d-1\\) and \\(e-1\\) equals \\(0,\\) making the product \\(0.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Expand \\((d-1)(e-1)\\) in terms of \\(d+e\\) and \\(de\\)",
        "Use Vieta’s formulas to find \\(d+e\\) and \\(de\\) without solving for the roots"
      ],
